#!/bin/bash
# mailserver/help.loc - site-aware usage (local only, read-only)

cat <<'EOF'
mailserver - the site mail store (Postfix + Cyrus IMAP + SpamAssassin + OpenDKIM)

Runs on the LAN mail host (uranus). Assumes a gateway built by the 'mailgate'
module (kjeib.com), linked by the WireGuard network named in mail.conf
(MAIL_WGNET), of which this host is the hub.

USAGE
  yamc -h uranus mailserver [-e yes=1]     report, then converge (idempotent)
  yamc -h uranus mailserver status         services, queue, cert expiry, DKIM, accounts
  yamc -h uranus mailserver dns            DNS rows to publish, and checks them (PASS/FAIL)
  yamc -h uranus mailserver user [NAME]    list accounts / set NAME's password
  yamc -h uranus -e delete=1 mailserver user NAME
  yamc -h uranus mailserver cert           pull the TLS cert now (the timer does it anyway)
  yamc -h uranus [-e save=1] mailserver key   show / record the cert-pull key (setup does it)

  As a role, with the tunnel hub:  yamcity -h uranus [-e yes=1] yamc.local/profiles/mailserver

CONFIGURATION  (yamc.local/mailserver/)
  mail.conf      public name, domains, LAN, gateway tunnel address, DKIM, limits
  aliases        address -> mailbox; anything not listed is refused
  certpull.pub   recorded by every setup run; mailgate installs it on the gateway

Each run ends with STILL TO DO: DKIM records to publish, missing passwords,
tunnel not up, certificate not yet pulled. 'dns' and 'user' are operations,
not configuration, so they stay separate commands.

Build and deploy order (store + gateway): yamc.local/mailserver/README.md
EOF
